  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is throwing a grand party at a bar. There is already a queue at the entrance, waiting for the event to start.\n\nThe queue can be represented as a string SSS consisting of NNN characters, each either 'B' (representing a boy) or 'G' (representing a girl).\n\nThe first character of the string represents the front of the queue. The entrance gate security allows people to enter one by one from the front of the queue, but as soon as the number of boys who have already entered the bar **exceeds twice** the number of girls, the security closes the entrance.\n\nYou have to determine the number of people in the queue who were allowed to enter the bar.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN — the length of SSS.\nThe next line contains the binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line a single integer denoting the number of people in the queue who were allowed to enter the bar.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1031 \\leq T \\leq 3\\cdot10^31≤T≤3⋅103",
      "1≤N≤101 \\leq N \\leq 101≤N≤10",
      "SSS is a string which contains only the characters `B` and `G`."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n8\nGBGBBBBG\n7\nBGGGGGG\n4\nGBBG",
        "output": "7\n1\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIn the first test case, after the first six people have entered, there are 444 boys and 222 girls. When the next boy enters, the security guard closes the gates immediately after, since the number of boys (555) now exceeds twice the number of girls (222) inside the bar.\n\n\nIn the second test case, after the first people has entered, there is 111 boy and 000 girls. The security guard closes the gates immediately since the number of boys (111) now exceeds twice the number of girls (000) inside the bar.\n\n\nIn the third test case, everyone was allowed to enter the bar."
      }
    ]
  },
